  "summary_en": "Working paper submitted to the CCW Group of Governmental Experts on LAWS by ten states. It reviews earlier GGE submissions and research on gender and racial bias in AI. It explains how such bias and the digital divide raise risks in autonomous weapons targeting, and it urges a future normative framework with positive obligations to mitigate bias.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Algorithmic gender and racial bias poses heightened risks in autonomous weapons, e.g., misrecognition of targets or miscategorising civilians as combatants.",
   "The GGE should recognise bias risks factually and develop measures to address them.",
   "Future framework should require comprehensive testing and reviews to identify and correct bias.",
   "Rigorous documentation of datasets for traceability and transparency, and benchmark testing against gender, age and race.",
   "Training and awareness for those testing and using the systems."
  ],
